Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/mediacodec: shed only AV1 temporal units that hold a single frame

av1_shed truncated a temporal unit to the OBUs before its last frame when
that frame was shown and refreshed no reference slot, so a unit carrying a
hidden alt-ref beside a non-reference shown frame went to the codec with
only the hidden frame. Every AV1 temporal unit has to show exactly one
frame; a unit without one is not a valid input.

The MediaTek decoder on a Fire TV Stick 4K Max (OMX.MTK.VIDEO.DECODER.AV1)
stops producing output once it is handed such units. Shedding runs while
mpv decodes up to an hr-seek target (AVDISCARD_NONREF), so resuming a 4K
AV1 film mid-file showed no frame and the player gave up after 30 s, three
times in a row; starting from the beginning, with hr-seek=no or with
hr-seek-framedrop=no, it played at once. In the 25 s around the resume
point (SVT-AV1 encode, 673 temporal units) 167 units were of that shape and
167 more held only the shed frame.

Keep a unit whole when anything besides its shed frame carries a frame or
sequence header; units that hold only the shed frame are still dropped.
VP9 superframe truncation is unchanged.

diff --git a/libavcodec/mediacodec_shed.c b/libavcodec/mediacodec_shed.c
index a269df4..a8269fb 100644
--- a/libavcodec/mediacodec_shed.c
+++ b/libavcodec/mediacodec_shed.c
@@ -342,16 +342,16 @@ static int av1_read(MediaCodecShedContext *sh, AVCodecContext *avctx,
     return 0;
 }
 
-// Shed the temporal unit's last frame when it is shown and refreshes no
-// reference slot. Earlier OBUs -- the temporal delimiter, hidden reference
-// frames, a sequence header -- are kept, so the decoder still consumes a
-// valid (if now frame-less) temporal unit; a unit that held nothing but the
-// shed frame is emptied instead.
+// Shed a temporal unit whose only frame is shown and refreshes no reference
+// slot. A unit that also carries a hidden reference frame or a sequence
+// header is kept whole: without its shown frame it would break the rule that
+// every temporal unit shows exactly one frame, and a MediaTek AV1 decoder
+// handed such a unit stops producing output.
 static int av1_shed(MediaCodecShedContext *sh, AVCodecContext *avctx, AVPacket *pkt)
 {
     CodedBitstreamFragment *frag = sh->frag;
     const AV1RawFrameHeader *hdr = NULL;
-    int last = -1, keep_units = 0, offset;
+    int last = -1;
 
     if (av1_read(sh, avctx, pkt) < 0)
         return 0;
@@ -374,20 +374,15 @@ static int av1_shed(MediaCodecShedContext *sh, AVCodecContext *avctx, AVPacket *
         hdr->frame_type == AV1_FRAME_KEY || hdr->frame_type == AV1_FRAME_SWITCH)
         goto keep;
 
-    offset = (int)(frag->units[last].data - frag->data);
-    if (offset < 0 || offset > pkt->size)
-        goto keep;
     for (int i = 0; i < last; i++) {
         CodedBitstreamUnitType type = frag->units[i].type;
         if (type == AV1_OBU_FRAME || type == AV1_OBU_FRAME_HEADER ||
             type == AV1_OBU_TILE_GROUP || type == AV1_OBU_TILE_LIST ||
             type == AV1_OBU_SEQUENCE_HEADER)
-            keep_units = 1;
+            goto keep;
     }
     ff_cbs_fragment_reset(frag);
-    // The buffer may be shared with the demuxer's cache: shorten the view,
-    // never write past it.
-    pkt->size = keep_units ? offset : 0;
+    pkt->size = 0;
     return 1;
 
 keep:
diff --git a/libavcodec/mediacodec_shed.h b/libavcodec/mediacodec_shed.h
index 41ceb2a..d0cf441 100644
--- a/libavcodec/mediacodec_shed.h
+++ b/libavcodec/mediacodec_shed.h
@@ -37,9 +37,10 @@
  * corrupt anything that follows; that is the whole safety argument, so
  * every helper fails open: anything it does not fully understand is kept.
  *
- * Reference frames that share an access unit with the shed frame (an AV1
- * hidden alt-ref, a VP9 superframe's hidden frames) stay in the packet; the
- * packet is truncated to them, never reordered.
+ * Hidden frames that share a VP9 superframe with the shed frame stay in the
+ * packet, which is truncated to them, never reordered. An AV1 temporal unit
+ * with a hidden frame beside its shown one is kept whole: every temporal unit
+ * has to show a frame.
  */
 
 typedef struct MediaCodecShedContext {
